From 5b2632a74cb975e3a5654f12d3bfdfafc88ba267 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 23:35:01 +0900
Subject: xen-troops working delta, rebased onto Xen 4.22

Reapply the EPAM rpi5_dev working delta on top of pristine xenbits stable-4.22
(d45d5687f1). The delta is the difference the rpi5_dev branch carries over its
own 4.19 base; it is squashed here because the individual commits do not rebase
independently (see the conflict notes below). It was first rebased onto
xen-troops xen-4.21-xt-gen5 (Xen 4.21.0) -- the 4.19 -> 4.21 notes below are
from that step and are kept because they explain the current shape -- and then
carried to 4.22, see the [4.22] note further down.

Conflict resolution highlights (4.19 -> 4.21):
- public/domctl.h: renumber to coexist with upstreamed 4.21 ops/flags
  (assign_static_11 87->91; CDF_directmap/staticmem ->(1U<<9)/(1U<<10)).
- arm/{domain,domctl}.c, common/{domctl,domain}.c: keep the libxl direct-map/
  static-mem (Stage 1) feature, adapt to 4.21 (domain_create flags arg,
  internal CDF_directmap/CDF_staticmem now upstream in xen/domain.h).
- arm/{irq,vgic}.c: keep the two SPI-passthrough behaviours the platform needs
  (a vGIC SPI-count floor and a trigger-type default), each behind its own
  Kconfig option; drop R-Car gsx branch (irrelevant to BCM2712).
- arm/domain_build.c: keep the hardware-domain SPI + device-MMIO capability
  grants, behind a Kconfig option; drop redundant sci_domain_init() (4.21 has
  its own SCI/SCMI framework).
- Drop as redundant/upstreamed: arm/sci/sci.c (moved to firmware/sci.c),
  the bulk dom0less-build.c additions, the inline SCI sanitise/init checks.

Not re-ported onto 4.21, because this configuration does not need them: the
dom0less console-drain change and the dt-overlay p2m_mmio_direct_dev override.

Every change to generic ARM behaviour is behind a Kconfig option that defaults
to n, so a build that does not select them gets unmodified upstream behaviour.
The options, all UNSUPPORTED-gated and declared in xen/arch/arm/Kconfig, are
XT_HWDOM_MMIO_DEVICE_ATTR, XT_HWDOM_PASSTHROUGH_CAPS (with
XT_HWDOM_IOMEM_CAP_START/END), XT_GUEST_MIN_NR_SPIS and
XT_GUEST_PASSTHROUGH_IRQ_TYPE_DEFAULT; each help text states the failure it
addresses. They are selected for this board by the recipe's
xen-config-rpi5-passthrough.cfg fragment.

Three relaxations the rpi5_dev delta carried in route_irq_to_guest(),
release_guest_irq() and vgic_reserve_virq() are not re-ported: with the SPI
floor in place each is equivalent to the upstream code it replaced, and the
release_guest_irq() rewrite additionally rejects the extended SPI range that
vgic_is_valid_line() accepts under CONFIG_GICV3_ESPI.

[4.22] Carried from 4.21.0 to 4.22.0. Of the 20 hunks across 13 files, 19 apply
to stable-4.22 with only offsets; one needed rebasing. Upstream e263eeaf71
("domctl: handle XEN_DOMCTL_{,un}bind_pt_irq without acquiring domctl lock") and
329edc090d ("domain: locking for irq_caps accesses") rewrote
arch_do_domctl()'s XEN_DOMCTL_bind_pt_irq from a chain of early returns into an
`rc = ...` if/else chain evaluated under read_lock(&currd->caps_lock), and
introduced a `currd` local for current->domain. The two diagnostic printks this
delta adds on the EPERM and EBUSY paths were moved into that shape; the only
textual change to the emitted code in the whole patch is
current->domain->domain_id -> currd->domain_id, which is the same value. Every
other added line across all 13 files is byte-identical to the 4.21 version, and
the six Kconfig options, their default-n/0 + UNSUPPORTED gating, and the three
un-ported relaxations described above are therefore unchanged. Applies to
stable-4.22 with zero fuzz, and builds clean (arm64): do_patch and do_compile both
succeed in the Yocto build for both Dom0 flavours (zephyr and thin-Linux), with
patch-fuzz left at ERROR.

Origin: https://github.com/xen-troops/xen branch rpi5_dev (tip 2214507e72),
 squashed and rebased onto branch xen-4.21-xt-gen5 (tip d4823d5ef9).
 Original authors of the squashed commits: Volodymyr Babchuk
 <volodymyr_babchuk@epam.com> and Ihor Usyk <ihor_usyk@epam.com> (EPAM Systems,
 GPL-2.0-only).
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream RPi5/BCM2712 working delta; local workaround, not upstreamable as-is]
